+# #558 — protected offline read snapshots
+
+## Infrastructure boundary (UI acceptance remains open)
+
+The owner’s #522 decision limits offline reads to Heute, Kontensalden, the current Vienna-month Plan and the latest fetched bookings. This implementation phase adds only the storage, request provenance and sign-out/transport boundary. The four consumer captures and a separate explicit read-only viewer are still pending. Existing authenticated routing, ledger calculations, mutation semantics, capture queue, service worker and cache policy are unchanged. No issue acceptance is claimed from these infrastructure tests alone.
+
+The intended snapshot is a completed successful response with its exact parameter key and fetch timestamp. Only the latest entry per approved view is retained in a separate same-origin IndexedDB database, `budget-read-snapshots`. Read authorization is not persisted: a cold offline copy must be a separately labelled, explicitly opened saved view, never evidence of a valid session. There is no invented TTL or session identifier.
+
+## Privacy and failure contract
+
+- Snapshot write permission starts disabled and is enabled only by a new successful real `/api/auth/status` response with `authenticated: true`. A response or request begun before a wipe cannot enable the replacement epoch. Query-cache auth values do not enable captures.
+- Sign-out immediately invalidates displayed copies and blocks new captures before waiting for the logout request. A shared nonfinancial logout-intent fence also rejects concurrent status responses and captures in other tabs and after cold reload while logout is pending. Each simultaneous logout owns a distinct random marker, so releasing one cannot clear another pending intent. An interrupted intent has no TTL and is cleared only by a real completed logout, fresh unauthenticated status or successful new login/recovery ceremony; an authenticated status alone cannot clear it. The final device wipe invalidates requests started during that interval. HTTP 401/403 and real unauthenticated status responses invalidate copies as well.
+- Every eligible GET starts an epoch token before fetching; only successful allowlisted read responses notify snapshot consumers. The observed payload is cloned before query consumers can mutate it optimistically. Auth/passkey responses, unrelated report endpoints and write payloads are not observed.
+- Same-tab generation checks, transactional persistent epochs, BroadcastChannel and a temporary nonfinancial localStorage wipe marker prevent late responses and other tabs from restoring a wiped copy. The marker contains only a random epoch, is removed after successful database erasure, and remains as a reload fence if erasure failed. Initialization clears any snapshot from the earlier epoch before allowing reads and rotates to a fresh epoch rather than rewinding to a stale marker. Inaccessible or read-only localStorage fences fail closed as well: initialization probes a nonfinancial write/removal before accepting financial copies, even if IndexedDB remains readable.
+- Unsupported IndexedDB immediately invalidates memory without impossible-store bookkeeping; an existing but blocked IndexedDB fails closed with bounded open/transaction waits; it neither prevents sign-out nor falls back to stale query data. Storage mechanisms fail independently. If all durable storage and messaging are inaccessible, physical erasure and immediate notification of another tab cannot be guaranteed; this follows the existing best-effort device-wipe boundary. No encryption, protection from same-origin script execution, unlocked-device access or browser-profile inspection is claimed.
+- Non-GET HTTP calls are denied before fetch while offline, while explicitly viewing a saved copy, or after a connection failure. While online and outside the saved viewer, an exact POST allowlist permits existing login/recovery/register/step-up and ordinary logout retries after a connection failure; passkey deletion, recovery-code regeneration and session administration remain blocked. Inside the viewer, the existing online idempotent `POST /api/bookings` replay is the sole exception; offline capture continues to persist in its existing queue. This guard supplements the future visibly disabled viewer controls; it does not replace server authorization.
+- No queued booking, capture-store schema, local financial preference list, app-shell cache, token, cookie, recovery code or passkey is added to the snapshot store or changed by its erasure. No API responses enter Cache Storage or the service worker.
+
+## Verification
+
+Frozen infrastructure validation (2026-10-19):
+
+- Focused Vitest: 8 files / 62 tests passed, including the new transport security cases and unchanged PWA, local-data, security panel, auth API, WebAuthn, stale-after-write and durable capture-queue suites. No existing test was edited.
+- Web typecheck, targeted ESLint and `npm run build:e2e` passed.
+- Native WebKit: all 7 security cases plus 3 canonical setup tests passed (10/10). Cases cover exact parameters/cold reload, request-start invalidation and old status, cross-tab wipe plus queue survival, failed erasure, cross-tab pending logout including reload, stale-marker epoch rewind, and read-only localStorage with readable native IndexedDB.
+- Independent Codex review of the complete frozen seven-file infrastructure diff found no actionable issue; its separate 4-file / 41-test HTTP/auth/WebAuthn/queue run passed. Source/test hashes stayed unchanged throughout review and native validation. This verifies the infrastructure boundary only.
+
+Commands:
+
+```sh
+npx vitest run apps/web/src/api/http-offline-security.test.ts apps/web/src/pwa/local-data.test.ts apps/web/src/pwa/pwa.test.tsx apps/web/src/pages/security-page.test.tsx apps/web/src/auth/api.test.ts apps/web/src/auth/webauthn.test.ts apps/web/src/auth/stale-after-write.test.ts apps/web/src/pwa/queue.test.ts --maxWorkers=1
+npm run typecheck -w @budget/web
+npm run build:e2e
+# Managed cloud runner, unchanged canonical project, real pinned WebKit:
+/workspace/.budget-tools/cloud-control/run-webkit.sh /workspace/cloud-offline-558 test e2e/issue-558-offline-store-security.spec.ts --project=webkit-iphone --workers=1
+```
+
+The repository-wide age check and final feature browser/visual acceptance remain pending until the consumer/viewer phase is complete. No final feature readiness or PR acceptance is claimed. Required final feature acceptance remains the four exact renderers (including completed displayed Depotwert), cold reload, warm draft preservation, explicit entry/clear, exact URL parameters/current Vienna month, amount privacy, read-only controls with the capture exception, route changes and desktop/mobile/real WebKit accessibility/layout checks. The infrastructure proof uses only literal synthetic values and native browser IndexedDB/BroadcastChannel; it does not substitute a system Chromium run for WebKit.
